---
title: The Man
description: Who writes v64otd.com, how each Dispatch is sourced, and how the site is funded.
---
## Who I Am

My name is DeWayne and I am located in North Fort Worth. I've spent more than twenty-five years inside enterprise technology: airlines, eCommerce, health insurance, private aviation and cloud infrastructure. My job was usually to sit between the customer and the people building the system, write down what was actually needed, and then watch what happened when a large organization made decisions by committee. I learned how systems fail. The failure is almost never technical.

I hold a Master's degree in IT Management. I also run [Vintage64TX](https://vintage64tx.com), a small consulting operation that moves people off aging, vendor-locked machines and onto Linux and simple websites they actually own.

## Why This Site Exists

Government fails the same way those organizations did. Bills get written for the people who fund campaigns, not the people who pay for the results, and both parties do it. This site is where I follow the money and the paper trail and write down what I find.

I don't belong to either party. When Washington fails, the record usually shows both sides had a hand in it, and I say so.

The site also has a personal side. [My Ledger](https://v64otd.com/ledger/) is where I write personal essays, including a series on my own seventeen-year medical story. The review sections cover gear, restaurants, recipes and places I've actually used, cooked or visited.

## How I Source a Dispatch

"The ledger doesn't lie" is the standard every Dispatch is built against.

- **Documents over quotes.** Court filings, agency reports, bill text and published contracts outrank anything secondhand. If a number appears in a Dispatch, I've traced where it came from, not just who repeated it last.
- **Two sources minimum.** No claim runs on one outlet's word. If I can't corroborate it, the piece says so, or it doesn't run.
- **Confidence is disclosed.** Each Dispatch says what's confirmed and what's directionally accurate, rather than presenting it all as equally certain.
- **Opinion is labeled.** My analysis appears under "My Take," separate from the reporting.
- **Verify before use.** Quotes, accounts and affiliations are checked before they're published. I tag officials and companies on social media only when the account is confirmed real.
- **Corrections are visible.** If I get a fact wrong, the piece is corrected and the correction is flagged at the top, not quietly edited.
- **Tips are leads, not sources.** Reader tips get checked against the public record before they become a Dispatch.

Not every section carries the same weight. Dispatches are held to the standard above. Reviews are hands-on testing. My Ledger is personal essay. The distinction is intentional.

## Reviews and Independence

I don't accept free products in exchange for a favorable review. If something fails, the review says it failed. Affiliate and referral links are disclosed wherever they appear, and they don't decide what gets recommended.

## Privacy

This site uses Google Analytics and Cloudflare analytics to count page views, general location and device type, and a Pinterest tag that measures visits coming from Pinterest. I don't sell your information. If you contact me, it stays with me. Details are in the [Privacy Policy](https://v64otd.com/pages/privacy-policy/).

